// ===========================================================================
// The monolith chamber: interior x -84.8..-33.6, z 4..55.2, floor 6.4,
// ceiling 57.6. A 51.2 m cube, hung off the west wall of the vault and reached
// from the far corner of the ledge behind the lava: a low corridor, then a
// stair climbing 6.4 m in a shaft that opens out above you.
//
// The crosses stop 9.6 m short of the ceiling, which is a good deal more than
// they stand clear of the floor: the roof wants dark above them rather than
// the tops of the arms crowding it.
//
// The door is left the size it always was, so the room opens out all at once
// as you step through it rather than being announced by its entrance.
//
// The room is lit only by what the crosses give off, which is little, by the
// well in the roof, and by one lamp inside the door. Everything else is meant
// to be lost in the dark.
// ===========================================================================

// --- The corridor in from the ledge, and the stair shaft beyond it ---
//
// The corridor is as wide as the ledge it leaves and the height of a door. The
// shaft it runs into is wider again and more than twice as tall, so the space
// opens out around you and over your head as the stair starts to climb.

