// --- The roof ---
//
// The slab is broken into coffers by eight ribs, 2.4 m across and hanging
// 3.2 m below it, and the middle square of that grid is left open: a well
// 12.8 m across and 19.2 m deep, capped by a bank of lamps.
//
// The ribs are set out from the opening rather than from the room, so the two
// either side of it frame it exactly and the coffers left over still come out
// even -- 7.2 m apiece, against the 12.8 m of the well.
//
// The well holds the only white light in the room, and it lands where it would
// fall: on the top of the monolith, which stands directly under it. Two lamps
// make it, since one cannot. The lamp up in the well shows the walls of the
// well, and a second below the mouth does the falling: light does not carry
// through the slab, so nothing above it can light what is below.

box   x0=-86.4 y0=57.6 z0=2.4 x1=-65.6 y1=59.2 z1=56.8 tex=metal_dark
box   x0=-52.8 y0=57.6 z0=2.4 x1=-32 y1=59.2 z1=56.8 tex=metal_dark
